<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n53599" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κᾰσίγνητ-ος</span></b> , ὁ,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάσις, γενέσθαι</span>, cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γνήσιος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>brother</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				8.585
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				9(1).867.6
			</span></i> (Corc., prob. <span class="entity">vi B.C.</span>), etc.; esp. of those
				<i>born from the same mother</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. καὶ ὄπατρον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					11.257
				</span></i>
			: later as fem., <i>sister</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τώδε
				τὼ κασιγνήτω</span> these two <i>sisters</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>El.</u>
				977
			</span></i>, cf. Ps.-<i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Philopatr.</u>
				11
			</span></i>: in more general sense, <i>cousin</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. τε ἔται τε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					16.456
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				15.545
			</span></i>: Astrol., <u>Gemini</u>, <i><span class="en">
				Doroth.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Heph.Astr.
				3.36
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> as
			Adj., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κασίγνητος, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">η</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span></span>, <i>brotherly, sisterly</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κασίγνητον κάρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ant.</u>
					899
				</span></i>
			,<i><span class="en">
				915
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				<u>El.</u>
				1164
			</span></i>, dub. l. in <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Or.</u>
				294
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κασιγνήτοιο φόνοιο</span> a
				<i>brother's</i> murder, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				9.567
			</span></i>. (Mostly poet.; also 
				Aeol.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Sapph.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				1.2
			</span></i> (prob.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12(2).526d19
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Eresus</span>), and
				<i><span class="en">Cypr.,
					<u>Inscr.Cypr.</u>135.3</span></i>
			H. (<span class="entity">Idalion</span>): Thess. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατίγνειτος</span></b> 
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				9(2).894
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Larissa</span>).)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
